In MQL5, you can manage your stop loss level with your risk management strategy using MetaTrader 5. For a stop loss set at 1% of your balance, you would need to write a code to adjust the lot size of your orders according to your available balance.

Firstly, please understand that interacting with your trading balance directly in your loss management system is viewed as a defensive strategy which stands against the basic idea of forex, that is, to realize profits by taking risks. However, below is a sample expert advisor code on how you can set your stop loss to be 1% of your trading balance:

```MQL5
double CalculateLotSize()
{
    double balance = AccountInfoDouble(ACCOUNT_BALANCE);
    double risk = 0.01; // Change this to set your risk level (1% in this case)
    double stopLossPips = 50; // Set your stop loss level in pips
    double pipValue = SymbolInfoDouble(Symbol(), SYMBOL_TRADE_TICK_VALUE);
    double stopLossMoney = balance * risk;
    double lotSize = stopLossMoney / (stopLossPips * pipValue);

    return lotSize;
}
```

In this sample algorithm:

- `AccountInfoDouble(ACCOUNT_BALANCE)` retrieves the current balance of the account.
- `risk` variable is set as the percent of your trading balance that you are prepared to risk on one trade. For you, this will be 1% (0.01).
- `SymbolInfoDouble(Symbol(), SYMBOL_TRADE_TICK_VALUE)` retrieves the profit value of the current or custom symbol for one pip or one point depending on the type of calculations.

Keep in mind that you need to adjust this to your case and incorporate this with your MQL5 strategy. Also, adjust "stopLossPips" to the actual stop loss that you intend to put for your trades.

This implementation makes certain assumptions such as equal weigh of different currency pairs which might not be always correct and exchange rate which is assumed as 1. Please customize this according to your need.

Remember, above code is the simplest version. It doesn't consider commission and slippage. You need to work more on it to suit your needs. Also, error handling of return values from MetaTrader 5 functions are omitted.

